  "question": {
    "text": "Let $k \\in \\mathbb{R}$. If $\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0^+}(\\sin (\\sin k x)+\\cos x+x)^{\\frac{2}{x}}=e^6$, then the value of $k$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "TsKFw",
      "text": "$1$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "hQwVm",
      "text": "$2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "dlpVD",
      "text": "$3$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LWcpv",
      "text": "$4$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "\\(\\begin{aligned} & l=\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0^{+}}(\\sin (\\sin k x)+\\cos x+x)^{\\frac{2}{x}}=e^6 \\\\ & \\Rightarrow \\ln l=\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0^{+}} \\frac{2}{x}(\\sin (\\sin k x)+\\cos x+x-1) \\\\ & \\Rightarrow \\ln l=\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0^{+}} 2\\left(\\frac{\\sin (\\sin k x)}{\\sin k x} \\cdot \\frac{\\sin k x}{k x} \\cdot \\frac{k x}{x}+1-\\frac{(1-\\cos x)}{x^2} \\cdot x\\right) \\\\ & \\Rightarrow \\ln l=2(k+1) \\\\ & \\Rightarrow l=e^{2(k+1)}=e^6 \\\\ & k+1=3 \\\\ & \\Rightarrow k=2\\end{aligned}\\)",
    "image": null
  },
